{
	title: 'Zero-dependency MCP client',
	spec: 'Hal calls tools of Model Context Protocol servers without third-party packages. Servers are configured in the home file mcp.ason as { mcpServers: { <name>: { command, args, env, cwd, timeout } | { url, headers, timeout } } } (the Claude/Cursor format); enabled: false skips one. ${NAME} in env and header values expands from the process environment, keeping credentials out of the file. Transports: stdio (newline-delimited JSON-RPC, child in its own process group) and streamable HTTP (JSON or SSE replies, Mcp-Session-Id, re-initialize on 404 of an expired session). A server starts on first use: initialize, notifications/initialized, paginated tools/list; tools/list_changed refreshes the list. The native tool MCP lists servers (MCP), a server tools with signatures (MCP "<server>"), and calls one (MCP "<server>.<tool>" { args }). Results keep text, images and resources; isError becomes a tool error. Tool calls are never retried; a crashed server restarts on the next call. Aborting a call sends notifications/cancelled. Requests time out after timeout seconds (default 60). Every failure shows the complete message, with the server stderr tail. /mcp shows each server state and tools; /mcp reconnect <name> restarts one. Servers stop when the host exits. No OAuth, resources, prompts, sampling or elicitation. Replaces mcporter.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Live-file arrays are proxies; child_process.spawn takes a proxied args array for its options argument, so mcp.ts copies args before spawning.',
		'A request rejected with HTTP 404 for a known Mcp-Session-Id is resent once in a new session: the server never processed it. Any other failure of tools/call is reported, never retried.',
		'Tool.readOnly is static, so every MCP call, listings included, runs as effectful (sequential).',
		'Checked by hand against chrome-devtools-mcp: 33 tools, about 8 kB listing, list_pages works, first start about 1.5 s with npx.'
	],
	needs: []
}
